kia: quick ping  i'm going to open a tiny PR to slim down the 429 troubleshooting page. it currently has three overlapping snippets and a stale SDK anchor. i'll replace with one canonical JS + one Python snippet, add a Retry-After parser note, and fix links. will push in ~10m.
tom: please make the JS snippet copy-pasteable using the hosted SDK call (exact params). we keep getting users pasting pseudo-retry loops. show `maxRetries`, `baseMs`, `capMs`, and `jitter`.
leena: add a one-line explainer under "fallback behavior": runtime trims input to fit model limits before fallback selection. that explains a lot of support tickets. also include a tiny ops note about when to prefer a model variant vs a quantized fallback.
doc-bot: linkcheck: broken link found in error-reference/429.md -> "/docs/sdk/retries-old" returned 404 (detected 3h ago)
kia: thanks bot  i'll point the SDK link to `/docs/sdk/retries-guide#policy-examples` and include a changelog entry. planning this compact JS example:
```js
// prefer Retry-After header, else capped exponential backoff with jitter
function parseRetryAfter(h) {
  if (!h) return null;
  const s = Number(h);
  if (!Number.isNaN(s)) return s * 1000;
  const t = Date.parse(h);
  return Number.isNaN(t) ? null : Math.max(0, t - Date.now());
}
await redwood.generate({
  model: 'redwood-small',
  input: prompt,
  retry: { maxRetries: 3, baseMs: 200, capMs: 5000, jitter: true }
});
// on 429: use parseRetryAfter(headers['retry-after']) || capped exp backoff
```
patrick: can you also add a minimal curl example for ops/customer copy-paste? even a two-line `sleep` pattern helps.
